mpensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Perimeter Solutions, SA is a mid-cap basic materials business with a $4.8B market cap on $653M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +22% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are contracting by -22.3pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 50%.","The business throws off $209M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 32 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","Accruals are elevated at -16.8% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, thin -5.1\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.8%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 9.0% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins contracting -22.3pp YoY \u2014 competitive pressure is eroding the franchise","sev":"red","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Price sits 45% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.45031894361885},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.7) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 40% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.6% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Heavy insider selling (net $232.9M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-232859106.94},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 53/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Trade policy and tariff whiplash \u2014 materials producers are first-order casualties of protectionist swings, and margin gets squeezed from both input and output pricing.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 353% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Gross margin tops the Basic Materials peer set \u2014 genuine pricing power is present here","Growing faster than most Basic Materials peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Strong Results Could Be A Game Changer For Perimeter Group (PRM)","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/materials/nyse-prm/perimeter-group/news/strong-results-could-be-a-game-changer-for-perimeter-group-p","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793968366.695,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.875,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Perimeter (PRM) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"fool.com","link":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/11/05/perimeter-prm-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/?source=iedfolrf0000001","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793908643.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.103,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Perimeter Group outlines $30M-$40M annual capex plan while accepting a period of \u201cdistressed adjusted EBITDA\u201d at PDI (NYSE:PRM)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4667116-perimeter-group-outlines-30m-40m-annu